    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Well, again, I think we've had some real successes in diversity in the party. In terms of elected officials, we have an African-American United States Senator. We have an Indian-American governor. In Louisiana, another Indian American governor in South Carolina, myself elected statewide, what you're talking about is electoral performance. That's a different issue and it's a serious one and it goes back to the point I made earlier. You have Americans that feel insecure about their economic future. They're struggling to get ahead despite working hard or they fear that their children will not have the opportunities they want. They see the Republican Party, unfortunately, they've been convinced many people that the Republican Party is the defender of those who have made it and that the Republican Party is not fighting on behalf of those who are trying to make it. I think we have to change that perception and the best way to change that perception is through concrete public policy solutions that address those hopes and those aspirations because I think we have answers for those things. We have not done a good enough job of consistently communicating",
