    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, I think our foreign policy should be strategic, not tactical. And in essence, I think too much of the foreign policy today around the world, not just the U.S., is determined simply on tactics. I think it needs to be strategic. And the strategic vision of the United States should have informed policies, first and foremost, to act in defense of our security and our safety. Second, in the promotion of our values around the world, including the values of free enterprise, the values of freedom of speech and freedom of liberty to live as one chooses. These are the values that I think we should promote. And then I think we should look for ways to use the power of the United States to convene like-minded nations, like the UK, to work with us, to achieve this in",
